<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Munda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">45 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caesars-civil-war">Caesar's Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Munda was fought on 17 March 45 BCE in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> and the Pompeian army of Gnaeus and Sextus Pompeius and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titus-labienus">Titus Labienus</a>. After a hard fight Caesar won; Labienus was killed, and Gnaeus Pompeius was caught and executed soon afterwards. It was Caesar's last battle of the civil war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-munda.jpg" alt="Battle of Munda" width="320" height="148" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Munda_(M._Merian).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
